  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "40",
  "quote": "No landlord shall, without legal process, seize a tenant’s property for default in the payment of rent or for the breach of any other obligation of the tenant.",
  "reason": "Section 40 of the Act abolishes the common law remedy of distress, prohibiting landlords from seizing a tenant's personal property for rent arrears without legal process. Any tenancy agreement term purporting to allow such seizure is contrary to the Act and void."
}

